{"module":"banking","voice":"female","duration":151.2,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Banking, insurance and taxes","start":0.0,"end":2.71,"words":[[0.05,0.66],[0.96,1.74],[1.74,2.0],[2.0,2.52]]},{"el":"intro","text":"The history of wealth is covered in its own module.","start":3.51,"end":6.48,"words":[[3.56,3.69],[3.69,4.15],[4.15,4.28],[4.28,4.55],[4.55,4.68],[4.68,5.01],[5.01,5.14],[5.14,5.34],[5.34,5.54],[5.54,6.0]]},{"el":"intro","text":"This one is about today: the ordinary financial systems where race still changes the price.","start":6.83,"end":12.78,"words":[[6.89,7.1],[7.1,7.31],[7.31,7.46],[7.46,7.81],[7.81,8.24],[8.49,8.63],[8.63,9.12],[9.12,9.76],[9.76,10.26],[10.26,10.47],[10.47,10.76],[10.76,11.04],[11.04,11.68],[11.68,11.82],[11.82,12.25]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Who gets a bank","start":13.13,"end":14.11,"words":[[13.17,13.31],[13.31,13.59],[13.59,13.73],[13.73,14.0]]},{"el":"s0","text":"In the FDIC's 2021 survey, about 11% of Black households had no bank account, compared with about 2% of white households.","start":14.81,"end":24.26,"words":[[14.86,15.0],[15.0,15.14],[15.14,15.49],[15.49,16.54],[16.54,16.96],[17.2,17.55],[17.55,18.39],[18.39,18.53],[18.53,18.81],[18.81,19.51],[19.51,19.72],[19.72,19.93],[19.93,20.21],[20.21,20.7],[20.95,21.44],[21.44,21.65],[21.65,22.0],[22.0,22.56],[22.56,22.7],[22.7,22.98],[22.98,23.75]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Without one, families pay more for check cashing and short-term loans.","start":24.61,"end":29.45,"words":[[24.65,25.14],[25.14,25.47],[25.76,26.34],[26.34,26.58],[26.58,26.75],[26.75,26.91],[26.91,27.24],[27.24,27.65],[27.65,27.9],[27.9,28.39],[28.39,28.89]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Black-owned banks and community development credit unions serve many of these neighborhoods; only about 20 Black-owned banks remain.","start":29.8,"end":37.76,"words":[[29.86,30.4],[30.4,30.74],[30.74,30.94],[30.94,31.55],[31.55,32.29],[32.29,32.69],[32.69,33.17],[33.17,33.37],[33.37,33.64],[33.64,33.77],[33.77,33.98],[33.98,34.65],[34.89,35.22],[35.22,35.56],[35.56,35.97],[35.97,36.51],[36.51,36.84],[36.84,37.32]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Mortgages","start":38.66,"end":39.87,"words":[[38.71,39.7]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Black and Latino borrowers pay higher mortgage rates than comparable white borrowers (Bartlett et al., 2022).","start":40.57,"end":46.75,"words":[[40.63,40.88],[40.88,41.06],[41.06,41.5],[41.5,41.93],[41.93,42.11],[42.11,42.36],[42.36,42.73],[42.73,43.04],[43.04,43.22],[43.22,43.84],[43.84,44.09],[44.09,44.52],[44.52,44.89],[44.89,45.01],[45.01,45.2],[45.41,46.34]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Lenders have paid large settlements over steering minority borrowers into costlier loans, including Countrywide (2011) and Wells Fargo (2012).","start":47.1,"end":57.36,"words":[[47.15,47.59],[47.59,47.8],[47.8,48.09],[48.09,48.39],[48.39,49.11],[49.11,49.4],[49.4,49.91],[49.91,50.57],[50.57,51.08],[51.08,51.37],[51.37,51.95],[51.95,52.39],[52.64,53.23],[53.23,53.95],[53.95,54.9],[55.15,55.37],[55.37,55.66],[55.66,56.03],[56.03,56.9]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Are approval algorithms biased?","start":58.26,"end":60.42,"words":[[58.31,58.38],[58.38,58.85],[58.85,59.52],[59.52,59.99]]},{"el":"s2","text":"A 2021 analysis by The Markup of public mortgage data found lenders were about 80% more likely to deny Black applicants than similar white applicants.","start":61.12,"end":70.4,"words":[[61.18,61.31],[61.31,62.29],[62.29,62.82],[62.82,63.02],[63.02,63.15],[63.15,63.47],[63.47,63.6],[63.6,64.0],[64.0,64.39],[64.39,64.72],[64.72,65.05],[65.05,65.44],[65.44,65.57],[65.57,65.9],[65.9,66.55],[66.55,66.68],[66.68,67.08],[67.08,67.21],[67.21,67.54],[67.54,67.8],[67.8,68.39],[68.39,68.58],[68.58,68.98],[68.98,69.24],[69.24,69.89]]},{"el":"s2","text":"The lending industry disputed it, noting the public data lacks credit scores.","start":70.75,"end":76.32,"words":[[70.79,70.94],[70.94,71.4],[71.4,72.01],[72.01,72.71],[72.71,72.94],[73.2,73.66],[73.66,73.82],[73.82,74.28],[74.28,74.66],[74.66,74.97],[74.97,75.43],[75.43,75.81]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Regulators and researchers continue to debate how much of the gap comes from bias in models versus differences in credit histories that themselves reflect past discrimination.","start":76.67,"end":88.03,"words":[[76.72,77.57],[77.57,77.8],[77.8,78.41],[78.41,79.03],[79.03,79.18],[79.18,79.65],[79.65,79.88],[79.88,80.19],[80.19,80.34],[80.34,80.49],[80.49,80.72],[80.72,81.03],[81.03,81.34],[81.34,81.73],[81.73,81.88],[81.88,82.34],[82.34,82.73],[82.73,83.42],[83.42,83.57],[83.57,84.04],[84.04,84.65],[84.65,84.88],[84.88,85.5],[85.5,86.04],[86.04,86.35],[86.35,87.5]]},{"el":"h3","text":"Appraisals, insurance and property taxes","start":88.93,"end":92.47,"words":[[88.98,89.84],[90.14,90.91],[90.91,91.17],[91.17,91.77],[91.77,92.29]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Homes in Black neighborhoods are appraised lower (see “Is racism over?”).","start":93.17,"end":97.35,"words":[[93.21,93.57],[93.57,93.72],[93.72,94.01],[94.01,94.67],[94.67,94.75],[94.75,95.26],[95.26,95.55],[95.55,95.7],[95.7,95.85],[95.85,96.43],[96.43,96.8]]},{"el":"s3","text":"A 2017 investigation by ProPublica and Consumer Reports found some insurers charged car insurance premiums as much as 30% higher in minority neighborhoods than in white neighborhoods with similar accident risk.","start":97.7,"end":114.62,"words":[[97.75,97.92],[97.92,99.18],[99.18,100.34],[100.34,100.61],[100.61,101.59],[101.59,101.86],[101.86,102.49],[102.49,103.02],[103.02,103.47],[103.47,103.74],[103.74,104.46],[104.46,104.99],[104.99,105.17],[105.17,105.98],[105.98,106.69],[106.69,106.87],[106.87,107.23],[107.23,107.41],[107.41,108.3],[108.3,108.66],[108.66,108.84],[108.84,109.65],[109.65,110.45],[110.45,110.72],[110.72,110.9],[110.9,111.26],[111.26,112.06],[112.06,112.33],[112.33,112.87],[112.87,113.58],[113.58,114.03]]},{"el":"s3","text":"And a 2022 study found Black and Hispanic homeowners pay about 10–13% more in property taxes than white homeowners with the same tax rate, because assessors overvalue cheaper homes relative to their sale prices.","start":114.97,"end":129.82,"words":[[115.02,115.25],[115.25,115.41],[115.41,116.48],[116.48,116.87],[116.87,117.25],[117.25,117.56],[117.56,117.79],[117.79,118.4],[118.4,119.09],[119.09,119.32],[119.32,119.71],[119.71,120.94],[120.94,121.09],[121.09,121.24],[121.24,121.78],[121.78,122.24],[122.24,122.47],[122.47,122.78],[122.78,123.47],[123.47,123.7],[123.7,123.85],[123.85,124.16],[124.16,124.47],[124.47,124.85],[125.12,125.5],[125.5,125.96],[125.96,126.66],[126.66,127.04],[127.04,127.42],[127.42,127.96],[127.96,128.11],[128.11,128.34],[128.34,128.65],[128.65,129.27]]},{"el":"h4","text":"What helps","start":130.72,"end":131.81,"words":[[130.77,131.11],[131.11,131.68]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Bank with Black-owned banks and community lenders, challenge low appraisals with comparable sales, appeal property assessments (free help is often available), and support enforcement of fair lending laws.","start":132.51,"end":145.39,"words":[[132.57,132.87],[132.87,133.1],[133.1,133.7],[133.7,134.08],[134.08,134.31],[134.31,134.98],[134.98,135.51],[135.77,136.38],[136.38,136.6],[136.6,137.28],[137.28,137.51],[137.51,138.26],[138.26,138.71],[138.98,139.28],[139.28,139.8],[139.8,140.48],[140.48,140.71],[140.71,141.01],[141.01,141.16],[141.16,141.46],[141.46,142.21],[142.48,142.7],[142.7,143.08],[143.08,143.76],[143.76,143.91],[143.91,144.13],[144.13,144.59],[144.59,144.89]]},{"el":"s4","text":"The quests “Bank with the community” and “Teach a money workshop” put this into practice.","start":145.74,"end":150.27,"words":[[145.79,145.92],[145.92,146.29],[146.29,146.55],[146.55,146.74],[146.74,146.86],[146.86,147.43],[147.43,147.62],[147.62,147.88],[147.88,148.0],[148.0,148.26],[148.26,148.63],[148.63,148.82],[148.82,149.01],[149.01,149.27],[149.27,149.77]]}]}